<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mahamuni Buddha</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mahamuni Image</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mahamuni Buddha is a seated bronze image of the Buddha, the most revered statue in Myanmar. Arakanese tradition says it was cast in the Buddha's lifetime for King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandrasuriya">Chandrasuriya</a> of Dhanyawadi, and it was the palladium of Arakanese kingdoms for centuries. In 1785 the Konbaung king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bodawpaya">Bodawpaya</a> conquered Arakan and carried it to his capital; it now stands in the Mahamuni Pagoda in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandalay">Mandalay</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mahamuni-buddha.jpg" alt="Mahamuni Buddha" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wagaung (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mahamuni_Image.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
